Additional Use Grant: Cann-o-Call Small-Business Production Use Grant

Qualifying users may use the Licensed Work in production without a commercial
license fee only if both of the following are true:

1. The user and its Affiliates have fewer than 50 full-time-equivalent
   employees in the aggregate; and
2. The user and its Affiliates have less than US $5,000,000 aggregate gross
   annual revenue.

“Affiliate” means an entity that directly or indirectly controls, is
controlled by, or is under common control with the user. Employee count and
gross annual revenue are aggregated across the user and all Affiliates.

Qualifying use includes the user's own internal business, organizational, and
operational use; qualifying nonprofit internal use; teaching; coursework;
academic research; and qualifying educational institutional use.

This Additional Use Grant does not permit hosted SaaS offered to third parties,
hosted Cann-o-Call service for third parties, managed services, managed
infrastructure sold to third parties, paid automation or agent operations for
third parties, resale, sublicensing as a commercial offering, rental or lease
of access, white-label offerings, or commercial service offerings in which
Cann-o-Call functionality forms a material part of the service sold. Those uses
require a separate commercial license.

If a previously qualifying user later exceeds either eligibility threshold, the
user may continue the existing previously permitted deployment for up to 30
days solely to obtain a commercial license or discontinue the newly
non-permitted use. During that period, the user may not materially expand the
deployment or create new deployments relying on this Additional Use Grant.

Nonprofit organizations may qualify for free internal production use only when
they satisfy the same eligibility thresholds. Educational institutions may use
the Licensed Work for teaching, coursework, academic research, and internal
institutional use only when otherwise eligible. Neither status permits the
hosted third-party, managed-service, resale, or white-label uses excluded
above.

